# ---------------------------------
#   ports/buildheaders — build-only ports other packages' headers include
# ---------------------------------
#
#   <port>...
#
# The ports of ports/buildonly whose headers, pkg-config files or protocol
# files the development files of another package include or require:
# libX11's X11/Xlib.h includes X11/X.h and its x11.pc requires xproto, both
# xorgproto's. The image leaves every one of them out, and a build here
# reaches none of them through an installed package, so before a build
# `kdos update` installs each one that a package the build compiles against
# names in `depends =`, prebuilt (dev_prepare in kdos-tools' update.c).
# Without it every build against that package fails to find its headers.
#
# A PORT HERE MUST BE IN ports/buildonly AND BE A PORT; preflight fails the
# tree otherwise. A port whose own run-time closure is large stays out:
# boost's numpy edge would put numpy and openblas on every such build. A line
# starting with '#' and a blank line are skipped.

